        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/eb8c5e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-12T21:08:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>McBehrer wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>The trick is to take out Set and Atum first.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Is that any different from non-challenge mode advanced/normal?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I know some people prefer not to take out set first when not doing a challenge mode game just because they don’t like the mandatory extra villain play, even though the heroes benefit more than the villains.</p>\n<p>Some people just hate fun I guess.</p>",
